    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 1,
        "line": 1,
        "text": "London in the 1960’s. Everyone had a story about the Krays. You could walk into any pub to hear a lie or two about them."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 1,
        "line": 888,
        "text": "Reggie spent 33 years in prison for killing Jack McVitie. Through all those years, until the end, he carried a pair of tickets with him. Reggie, my prince, we were supposed to go to Ibiza after all."
      }
